fix(agent): replay a session's history when the client asks for it

`run --session KEY "message"` attaches to a session that already has a history
and the client starts blank, so it wants the transcript. It got none: the replay
hung on the request having no message, which is true for a resume and false for
every other turn, so the one case that sends a message to an existing session
was the one case with nothing to show.

The request now says so itself. `SendMessage` carries `replay`, the client sets
it when it is attaching to a session it has not shown, and the service acts on
what it is told instead of inferring intent from the shape of the request.
`run --session` asks for it; the interactive prompt does not, because the
transcript is already on screen and replaying it would print the conversation
twice.

`Resume` keeps replaying without the flag, because showing where the
conversation was is what a resume is for.
